From 815a9bb20f6477dc1f1f6d3404f4772accca7f02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 13:47:57 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] The window can be made where it's told (WOW_WINDOW_AT) (patch
 0086)

`WOW_WINDOW_AT=<x>,<y>` makes the primary window at that desktop position, its outer top-left in
physical pixels of the whole desktop (negative left of or above the primary monitor). A harness
filming on another monitor then gets the window there from its first frame: until now it opened
where Windows put it and only moved once the client answered a move, about 1.4 s in (after the
graphics start), and Windows' STARTF_USEPOSITION hint isn't honoured.

The position goes in the `Window` the app is built with (`WindowPosition::At`). winit makes the
window hidden, sizes it, moves it there and only then is it shown, so it never shows on the primary
screen. Physical pixels need no scale factor, so it holds on a monitor of another DPI: winit's
WM_DPICHANGED keeps the window's top-left on the new monitor and rescales its size there.

`bevy_winit` places only a windowed window; a fullscreen one is born on the `Primary` monitor. So a
player whose mode is fullscreen (or maximized) is born windowed at the position when it is set, and
`apply_window_mode`'s first run makes the window fullscreen on the monitor it stands on (`Current`,
as every live toggle already does). A `RestartGx()` and a later windowed/fullscreen toggle keep to
the window's own monitor as before. The no-pixel probe parking (`WOW_PROBE_PARK`) is unchanged.

Unset or unparsable (anything but two integers and a comma): exactly today's behaviour.
